      "text": "Let's break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. **Determine the total miles driven:** The odometer reading went from 74,568 miles to 74,592 miles. Thus, the miles driven is:\n\\[ 74,592 \\text{ meters} - 74,568 \\text{ meters} = 24 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the amount of gas used:** Given that Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon and the price of one gallon of gas is $\\$4.05$, the total gas used in gallons is:\n\\[ 24 \\text{ miles} \\div 28 \\text{ miles per gallon} \\approx 0.8571 \\text{ gallons} \\]\n\n3. **Compute the total cost of gas:** The cost of gas used in dollars is:\n\\[ 0.8571 \\text{ gallons} \\times \\$4.05 \\text{ dollars per gallon} \\approx 3.47 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas is $ \\$3.47$, rounded to the nearest cent:\n\nLet's use Python to verify these computations.\n```python\n# Parameters\r\ninitial_odometer = 74568\r\nfinal_odometer = 74592\r\nmiles_per_gallon = 28\r\nprice_per_gallon = 4.05\r\n\r\n# Calculate total miles driven\r\ntotal_miles_driven = final_odometer - initial_odometer\r\n\r\n# Calculate the amount of gas used in gallons\r\ngas_used_gallons = total_miles_driven / miles_per_gallon\r\n\r\n# Calculate the total cost of gas in dollars\r\ntotal_gas_cost = gas_used_gallons * price_per_gallon\r\n\r\n# Round to the nearest cent\r\ntotal_gas_cost_rounded = round(total_gas_cost, 2)\r\n\r\nprint(total_gas_cost_rounded)\n```\n```output\n3.47\n```\nThe cost of the gas that was used to drive Ryosuke back home from work is \\(\\boxed{3.47}\\) dollars.",
